# React Implementation Guidelines

<rule>
name: atlas_react
description: Standards for implementing proper React components and patterns
filters:
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\\.(?:jsx|tsx)$"
  - type: content
    pattern: "(?i)react|component|hook|jsx|props"

actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      When implementing React code:

      ## Component Structure
      - Use props interfaces
      - Use functional components with hooks
      - Prefer arrow functions when possible
      - Implement proper prop typing
      - Use proper state management
      - Implement proper effect handling
      - Follow component best practices

      ## Hooks Usage
      - Use proper dependency arrays
      - Implement custom hooks for reusable logic
      - Use proper hook ordering
      - Implement proper cleanup in useEffect
      - Follow hooks best practices

      ## Performance Optimization
      - Use React.memo for expensive components
      - Implement useCallback for function props
      - Use useMemo for expensive calculations
      - Implement proper key usage in lists
      - Follow performance best practices

      ## State Management
      - Use proper context implementation
      - Implement proper reducer patterns
      - Use proper state lifting
      - Implement proper prop drilling avoidance
      - Follow state management best practices

      ## Component Composition
      - Use proper component composition
      - Implement proper children usage
      - Use proper render props
      - Implement proper HOC patterns
      - Follow composition best practices

examples:
  - input: "Creating a new React component"
    output: "Component uses functional style, proper hooks, and follows React best practices"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
</rule> 